1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:01,434
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,534 --> 00:00:03,069
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,403 --> 00:00:05,605
(Episode 30)

4
00:00:07,374 --> 00:00:10,076
I need to sell this too.

5
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:13,380
Nothing's been moving lately.

6
00:00:14,214 --> 00:00:16,916
Would you get anything for it?

7
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:25,125
Could you lend me some money?

8
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:28,928
- My Ji Ni has nowhere to go...
- How would you pay it back?

9
00:00:29,062 --> 00:00:31,315
Byeon. I'll find him, I swear.

10
00:00:31,398 --> 00:00:34,601
And I'm thinking
of teaching private lessons again.

11
00:00:34,734 --> 00:00:37,037
- You know how good I am.
- Your hands are shaking.

12
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:40,940
They're not! I've just been run down.

13
00:00:41,107 --> 00:00:44,461
I may have quit,
but I'm trained in this. I can tell.

14
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:46,046
It isn't that bad.

15
00:00:46,179 --> 00:00:48,648
Maybe I practiced too hard all at once...

16
00:00:48,848 --> 00:00:50,917
Well...

17
00:00:51,084 --> 00:00:53,853
My husband hates lending money...

18
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,356
Please. I'm asking you.

19
00:00:59,125 --> 00:01:01,594
Excuse me. I need to take this call.

20
00:01:02,962 --> 00:01:04,664
Yes, hello?

21
00:01:04,998 --> 00:01:06,366
One moment.

22
00:01:14,941 --> 00:01:16,242
It's me.

23
00:01:16,543 --> 00:01:17,977
The rumors are all true!

24
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:20,180
You were right. She's being punished.

25
00:01:21,848 --> 00:01:24,451
Anyone who breaks up a family
shouldn't prosper.

26
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:27,153
She's living apart from her daughter, too.

27
00:01:27,787 --> 00:01:30,440
That girl suffered her whole life
for having the parents she did,

28
00:01:30,523 --> 00:01:32,425
and now she's struggling for money.

29
00:01:32,859 --> 00:01:34,761
I'll call you back, sweetheart.

30
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:39,599
It was my daughter.

31
00:01:41,701 --> 00:01:45,371
Did you tell your daughter I'm punished
for being the other woman?

32
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:48,675
I said no such thing.

33
00:01:48,842 --> 00:01:52,312
Whether I'm being punished or rewarded,
that's for me to deal with.

34
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:54,214
Who are you to judge me?

35
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:59,385
I was so desperate I asked for money
for the first time in my life, and this?

36
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,122
Isn't that a little cruel?

37
00:02:02,388 --> 00:02:04,858
How much did my husband help you
when you were struggling?

38
00:02:06,726 --> 00:02:08,728
I am grateful for that.

39
00:02:12,665 --> 00:02:15,235
I can't lend you money.

40
00:02:17,704 --> 00:02:19,205
But take this. It's the least I can do.

41
00:02:57,744 --> 00:02:59,546
There's nothing I can do for you.

42
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:02,348
I just wanted you to have a proper meal.

43
00:03:02,982 --> 00:03:04,117
Yeong Ju.

44
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:08,521
Do you think I'm being punished too?

45
00:03:08,922 --> 00:03:11,691
Who says you're being punished?

46
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,026
Well.

47
00:03:13,893 --> 00:03:15,328
I mean...

48
00:03:15,495 --> 00:03:17,764
You're certainly not being rewarded.

49
00:03:18,431 --> 00:03:20,500
So that's what you think as well.

50
00:03:20,833 --> 00:03:22,352
That's not it.

51
00:03:22,435 --> 00:03:25,405
I don't think that way anymore.
I told you.

52
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:28,174
Your daughter taught me a lot.

53
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:31,544
Honestly, now that he's gone,

54
00:03:31,778 --> 00:03:34,514
you and I have nothing left between us.

55
00:03:35,081 --> 00:03:39,552
Ji Ni saved O Reum's life,

56
00:03:39,652 --> 00:03:41,454
so I only think of how grateful I am.

57
00:03:41,754 --> 00:03:43,623
Don't read anything else into it.

58
00:03:48,061 --> 00:03:49,562
Hello.

59
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:52,865
They're just back from the hospital.

60
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:54,467
What did the doctor say?

61
00:03:54,601 --> 00:03:55,935
He said everything's fine.

62
00:04:07,614 --> 00:04:10,083
So that's where my daughter's marrow is.

63
00:04:10,817 --> 00:04:12,719
Yes.

64
00:04:12,952 --> 00:04:15,588
Thank you. I won't forget it.

65
00:04:17,056 --> 00:04:19,776
Yeong Ju, I can't eat feeling like this.

66
00:04:19,859 --> 00:04:21,578
What? Why not?

67
00:04:21,661 --> 00:04:24,564
Se Ri!

68
00:04:29,168 --> 00:04:31,104
What was that about?

69
00:04:31,371 --> 00:04:33,072
I have no idea.

70
00:04:33,172 --> 00:04:36,776
She asked if I thought
she was being punished...

71
00:04:36,976 --> 00:04:39,545
so I said she wasn't exactly
being rewarded.

72
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:42,582
- I couldn't very well lie.
- Of course not!

73
00:04:43,182 --> 00:04:46,352
At least she has a conscience.
She must know it herself.

74
00:04:46,686 --> 00:04:48,321
What was I supposed to say?

75
00:04:48,521 --> 00:04:51,591
"Everything's fine." "It's nothing."
Was I supposed to say that?

76
00:04:52,725 --> 00:04:55,828
I still dream about it and cry all night
until I'm drained.

77
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:57,530
Mother...

78
00:04:57,830 --> 00:05:00,533
Time is so cruel.

79
00:05:02,168 --> 00:05:04,437
She must have come back.

80
00:05:11,044 --> 00:05:12,912
- Come on in.
- Yes.

81
00:05:14,247 --> 00:05:16,616
What brings you here?

82
00:05:16,916 --> 00:05:19,236
I heard the boy was discharged,

83
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,904
so I stopped by on my way past.

84
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:22,455
Congratulations!

85
00:05:22,722 --> 00:05:24,290
Thank you.

86
00:05:24,590 --> 00:05:27,060
- Thank you so much.
- My pleasure.

87
00:05:31,397 --> 00:05:33,066
You too?

88
00:05:34,801 --> 00:05:38,371
Hearing that woman went under
had me laughing even in my sleep.

89
00:05:38,905 --> 00:05:43,109
I wish she'd gone under while Cha Min Ki
was still alive. What a shame.

90
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:46,546
Honestly...

91
00:06:12,171 --> 00:06:13,873
You were right. She's being punished.

92
00:06:14,006 --> 00:06:16,776
Anyone who breaks up a family
shouldn't prosper.

93
00:06:17,276 --> 00:06:19,312
She's living apart from her daughter, too.

94
00:06:19,979 --> 00:06:22,749
That girl suffered her whole life
for having the parents she did...

95
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:24,517
and now she's struggling for money.

96
00:06:25,752 --> 00:06:28,621
Do you think I'm being punished too?

97
00:06:29,589 --> 00:06:32,558
You're certainly not being rewarded.

98
00:06:40,199 --> 00:06:42,969
Ji Ni, I'm so sorry.

99
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:12,832
Your pulse is very weak.

100
00:07:12,965 --> 00:07:14,634
What's happening? Why is this?

101
00:07:14,867 --> 00:07:17,537
This hand is shaking a little.

102
00:07:17,670 --> 00:07:20,807
I have no strength.
I can't grip the strings.

103
00:07:21,541 --> 00:07:22,875
What's wrong with me?

104
00:07:23,042 --> 00:07:25,011
I have to start teaching again.

105
00:07:25,344 --> 00:07:26,396
Please help me.

106
00:07:26,479 --> 00:07:28,114
You're completely worn out.

107
00:07:28,714 --> 00:07:30,450
Go to a hospital and get it checked out.

108
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:31,835
Please wait a moment.

109
00:07:31,918 --> 00:07:33,286
I'll prepare some medicine.

110
00:07:37,657 --> 00:07:40,726
Now even my own body
is costing me money...

111
00:07:41,093 --> 00:07:42,328
Honestly.

112
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,033
Excuse me...

113
00:07:48,501 --> 00:07:51,471
Take this first.
I'll send the herbal tonic up shortly.

114
00:07:52,071 --> 00:07:54,073
Sa Bin, I've moved.

115
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:57,343
I'll come pick the medicine up,
so don't send it to the house.

116
00:07:58,244 --> 00:07:59,378
Sorry?

117
00:08:00,413 --> 00:08:01,981
How could it happen overnight...

118
00:08:02,114 --> 00:08:03,916
Overnight is exactly how it happened.

119
00:08:04,617 --> 00:08:06,336
If I'm going to make a living somehow,

120
00:08:06,419 --> 00:08:08,120
I need to stop the shaking fast.

121
00:08:11,090 --> 00:08:12,758
Forgive me for asking, but...

122
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:14,760
should I try to raise some money for you?

123
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:19,866
Everyone's afraid I'll ask them for money.

124
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:22,535
You really are a good man, Sa Bin.

125
00:08:24,103 --> 00:08:27,240
Someone told me I'm being punished.

126
00:08:28,374 --> 00:08:30,109
I'll take that punishment.

127
00:08:30,776 --> 00:08:34,347
That way my sins won't pass
down to my daughter.

128
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,749
Who would say something so vile?

129
00:08:37,149 --> 00:08:39,018
Don't associate with people like that.

130
00:08:39,585 --> 00:08:40,853
Thank you for the kind words.

131
00:08:41,387 --> 00:08:44,524
Put the medicine on my tab.
I'll pay you back somehow.

132
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,792
Don't say that. That hurts.

133
00:08:47,693 --> 00:08:48,828
I'm off.

134
00:08:49,595 --> 00:08:51,230
Se Ri...

135
00:08:51,898 --> 00:08:54,166
I'll stay strong. I'm Na Se Ri.

136
00:08:54,667 --> 00:08:57,603
I've been through far worse.
Don't worry about me.

137
00:09:12,084 --> 00:09:13,286
Unbelievable...

138
00:09:18,090 --> 00:09:20,192
I knew it.

139
00:09:20,359 --> 00:09:23,462
It's a pigsty.

140
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:33,673
Leaving food out like this...

141
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,876
And these socks.

142
00:09:41,847 --> 00:09:43,950
Honestly.

143
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:51,324
Justice prevails!

144
00:09:53,693 --> 00:09:55,861
Hey, raise your glasses!

145
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,663
You don't like your drink?
Say it with me. Justice...

146
00:09:57,897 --> 00:09:59,031
Say it!

147
00:09:59,165 --> 00:10:00,132
Justice...

148
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:01,317
Justice...

149
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:02,886
I can't hear you.

150
00:10:02,969 --> 00:10:04,637
Didn't you two serve in the army?

151
00:10:04,971 --> 00:10:07,640
Justice prevails!

152
00:10:07,907 --> 00:10:09,542
Justice prevails!

153
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:20,403
Marrow is one thing.

154
00:10:20,486 --> 00:10:23,206
She's your own flesh and blood,
so any decent person would have done it.

155
00:10:23,289 --> 00:10:25,992
Me? I'm not even grateful.

156
00:10:26,158 --> 00:10:29,528
- Il Dong.
- There's no need to grovel like that.

157
00:10:29,762 --> 00:10:32,999
When it comes down to it,
she's still that woman's daughter.

158
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:36,469
Il Dong. Seung Hyun hates hearing that.

159
00:10:36,702 --> 00:10:40,673
Like mother, like daughter.
And like father, like sons.

160
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:43,209
Well, that's true.

161
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:49,081
My brothers... no, my nephews.

162
00:10:49,649 --> 00:10:51,450
Your father...

163
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:54,720
that man was a sly fox.

164
00:10:54,887 --> 00:10:56,940
Having a child with another woman?

165
00:10:57,023 --> 00:10:59,759
Thank you. Truly.

166
00:10:59,859 --> 00:11:01,661
Let's call it even. Okay?

167
00:11:01,861 --> 00:11:03,462
- Have some food.
- What?

168
00:11:03,763 --> 00:11:07,266
I can't stand people
who eat while they drink.

169
00:11:07,466 --> 00:11:09,902
Liquor is liquor, food is food.

170
00:11:11,103 --> 00:11:14,340
Il Dong, you really never change.

171
00:11:15,875 --> 00:11:17,343
Smile, guys!

172
00:11:17,543 --> 00:11:19,445
Today is a good day.

173
00:11:19,578 --> 00:11:22,348
Cha Min Ki, that bastard, is gone!

174
00:11:22,548 --> 00:11:24,984
Just knowing I don't have
to share the same air...

175
00:11:25,151 --> 00:11:27,003
with that man,

176
00:11:27,086 --> 00:11:29,522
I can finally breathe again.

177
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:32,258
I feel the same way.

178
00:11:34,493 --> 00:11:37,463
But now there's no one left to rage at.

179
00:11:37,830 --> 00:11:39,699
- I kind of miss it.
- Exactly.

180
00:11:39,799 --> 00:11:41,751
As we go through life,

181
00:11:41,834 --> 00:11:44,520
you need someone to hate...

182
00:11:44,603 --> 00:11:46,839
to keep you going. Right?

183
00:11:47,773 --> 00:11:49,175
You are.

184
00:11:49,408 --> 00:11:52,378
How is the General these days?

185
00:11:52,478 --> 00:11:53,879
Of course he's well!

186
00:11:54,246 --> 00:11:56,315
If not for him,

187
00:11:56,649 --> 00:11:59,369
I'd have ended up in the brig or prison.

188
00:11:59,452 --> 00:12:03,656
I'll respect him
and serve him until I die.

189
00:12:03,789 --> 00:12:05,341
Introduce us sometime.

190
00:12:05,424 --> 00:12:07,159
Introduce you? All right.

191
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,829
Seung Hyun.

192
00:12:10,196 --> 00:12:12,131
Drink up.

193
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:13,449
It's refreshing.

194
00:12:13,532 --> 00:12:18,204
Just imagining that woman ruined
and wandering the streets feels so good.

195
00:12:19,205 --> 00:12:22,675
I was so pleased I even bought flowers.

196
00:12:22,775 --> 00:12:25,244
Have you ever seen me buy flowers?

197
00:12:25,377 --> 00:12:28,447
This is a celebration. A real celebration.

198
00:12:31,117 --> 00:12:33,352
Who's up for karaoke?

199
00:12:36,889 --> 00:12:38,491
When I was left on my own,

200
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:41,994
he deserted with a gun,
swearing he'd kill your father-in-law.

201
00:12:42,194 --> 00:12:45,731
I chased after him for ages
to keep him out of the brig.

202
00:12:45,931 --> 00:12:48,534
He's got quite a temper!

203
00:12:48,667 --> 00:12:50,836
Send him home fast.
It'll be trouble if he drinks more.

204
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:53,839
I will. I'll text Seung Hyun on the sly.

205
00:12:59,812 --> 00:13:02,381
Be good to Do Hee.

206
00:13:03,249 --> 00:13:06,018
There's plenty about her
that I don't care for either,

207
00:13:06,752 --> 00:13:10,356
but no matter how I look at it,
no one compares to Do Hee.

208
00:13:10,489 --> 00:13:12,825
- This is about Ambassador Do, isn't it?
- She loves you, too.

209
00:13:14,026 --> 00:13:15,761
Rather than someone you love,

210
00:13:16,028 --> 00:13:19,298
it's easier to live with someone
who loves you.

211
00:13:19,999 --> 00:13:22,802
She posted a bag on Instagram.
Did you buy it for her?

212
00:13:23,669 --> 00:13:25,371
No. Where would I get that kind of money?

213
00:13:25,905 --> 00:13:27,573
- She bought it herself.
- Well...

214
00:13:28,107 --> 00:13:29,975
She's not really on your level.

215
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:32,645
And what's my level?

216
00:13:32,745 --> 00:13:35,414
You really ought to be with an artist.

217
00:13:36,115 --> 00:13:38,751
When I heard you'd met a woman
studying art in England...

218
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:42,288
I thought it was a good thing.

219
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:46,625
But Do Hee doesn't paint, does she?

220
00:13:48,227 --> 00:13:50,296
You seem torn about something.

221
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,298
Don't be.

222
00:13:52,731 --> 00:13:53,699
I've decided...

223
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:56,669
to focus on Do Hee again.

224
00:13:58,204 --> 00:13:59,271
All right.

225
00:13:59,839 --> 00:14:03,275
Rather than acting like some mad artist,

226
00:14:04,043 --> 00:14:06,946
it's better to spend like Do Hee. Got it?

227
00:14:07,813 --> 00:14:09,381
Sleep well.

228
00:14:11,317 --> 00:14:12,585
You too, Mom.

229
00:14:18,757 --> 00:14:21,927
You really ought to be with an artist.

230
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:36,876
What is this?

231
00:14:43,616 --> 00:14:44,817
Who else but your mother?

232
00:14:45,017 --> 00:14:47,286
Who else would clean your room?

233
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:50,189
No, I'm on my way in.

234
00:14:50,522 --> 00:14:52,408
Make sure you lock up.

235
00:14:52,491 --> 00:14:53,826
That place isn't safe.

236
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,312
All right.

237
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:57,613
Just bear with it today.

238
00:14:57,696 --> 00:14:59,365
I'll move you out soon.

239
00:15:00,532 --> 00:15:02,801
Anyway, that's how it's going to be.

240
00:15:04,803 --> 00:15:05,871
Fine.

241
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:14,713
Honey.

242
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:16,582
Our daughter Ji Ni...

243
00:15:16,849 --> 00:15:19,385
I'll protect her to the end. Don't worry.

244
00:15:20,419 --> 00:15:22,721
I'm Na Se Ri.

245
00:16:09,234 --> 00:16:10,235
Yeong Ju.

246
00:16:10,436 --> 00:16:11,870
You said we should live together.

247
00:16:12,104 --> 00:16:13,105
So here I am.

248
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:17,491
- Se Ri...
- You said you'd give me anything.

249
00:16:17,743 --> 00:16:18,877
Give me this room.

250
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:20,346
It was empty last time I was here.

251
00:16:20,446 --> 00:16:22,748
- I'll take it. That's fine, isn't it?
- Excuse me!

252
00:16:23,082 --> 00:16:24,400
No matter how hard things get,

253
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:26,185
- you can't just move in here.
- Why not?

254
00:16:27,052 --> 00:16:28,638
Every time he came here,

255
00:16:28,721 --> 00:16:31,390
he said he was going home,
and it drove me mad.

256
00:16:31,523 --> 00:16:33,926
If it's his family home, it's mine too.

257
00:16:41,033 --> 00:16:42,034
Mom.

258
00:16:42,234 --> 00:16:44,103
What is this? Get out here!

259
00:16:48,841 --> 00:16:51,844
- Miss.
- Yes, sweetheart!

260
00:16:52,411 --> 00:16:56,515
So here's the boy
who took my daughter's marrow.

261
00:16:57,182 --> 00:17:00,152
I'm your real grandmother, you know.

262
00:17:02,588 --> 00:17:04,523
Compared to a grandmother
who couldn't donate,

263
00:17:04,723 --> 00:17:06,825
don't I have more right to you?

264
00:17:07,192 --> 00:17:08,560
Am I wrong?

265
00:17:25,511 --> 00:17:27,112
This is maddening.

266
00:17:27,413 --> 00:17:28,714
If we back down now,

267
00:17:28,847 --> 00:17:30,616
we'll actually be living together.

268
00:17:31,083 --> 00:17:33,852
Does that make sense? In 2026?

269
00:17:34,953 --> 00:17:36,822
This family is already a mess...

270
00:17:37,523 --> 00:17:39,958
Just pay her to leave.

271
00:17:40,125 --> 00:17:41,644
Then hand over your severance.

272
00:17:41,727 --> 00:17:43,095
My medical bills were huge.

273
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:44,830
You have insurance.

274
00:17:45,297 --> 00:17:47,199
And how many years have I even worked?

275
00:17:47,332 --> 00:17:48,901
How much severance could there be?

276
00:17:49,034 --> 00:17:51,036
I hate this as much as you do,

277
00:17:51,303 --> 00:17:53,138
but there's Ji Ni. What can I do?

278
00:17:53,639 --> 00:17:54,873
Somehow, within a month...

279
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:56,225
something will work out.

280
00:17:56,308 --> 00:17:57,526
She says she's teaching again.

281
00:17:57,609 --> 00:17:58,977
That's exactly my point.

282
00:17:59,178 --> 00:18:01,880
Mai keeps insisting
we should bring Ji Ni over right away.

283
00:18:02,014 --> 00:18:04,283
Then give her your room.

284
00:18:05,417 --> 00:18:06,418
You two!

285
00:18:06,652 --> 00:18:09,121
I said I'd throw you both out
if you fought in front of me.

286
00:18:09,288 --> 00:18:11,056
For O Reum,

287
00:18:11,256 --> 00:18:13,625
I stayed up all night on the paperwork.

288
00:18:14,226 --> 00:18:16,728
Am I someone who pulls all-nighters
at that man's company?

289
00:18:17,262 --> 00:18:18,797
You've come this far. Finish it.

290
00:18:21,967 --> 00:18:23,335
Yeong Ju, what are you doing?

291
00:18:24,103 --> 00:18:25,321
The three of you...

292
00:18:25,404 --> 00:18:27,339
What are you scheming now?

293
00:18:27,573 --> 00:18:28,841
I'm not leaving. Give it up!

294
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,776
I knew you weren't in your right mind,

295
00:18:30,976 --> 00:18:32,611
but please respect some boundaries.

296
00:18:32,845 --> 00:18:35,013
Are you a sociopath, by any chance?

297
00:18:35,881 --> 00:18:37,516
- Seung Woo.
- That's going too far.

298
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:39,651
It's my husband's family home,

299
00:18:39,751 --> 00:18:40,903
and my daughter's own blood is here.

300
00:18:40,986 --> 00:18:43,155
- Why can't I come?
- Don't be absurd!

301
00:18:43,889 --> 00:18:46,042
We're only letting you stay
because you're in a difficult situation.

302
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:47,726
It isn't a right you're owed.

303
00:18:48,026 --> 00:18:49,795
Never call it your husband's home again!

304
00:18:50,095 --> 00:18:51,797
You're killing what sympathy I had.

305
00:18:52,197 --> 00:18:53,465
Enough.

306
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:56,335
I'll raise the money, so get out.

307
00:18:57,469 --> 00:18:59,004
Do you really have to be like this?

308
00:18:59,238 --> 00:19:01,340
Yes. I really...

309
00:19:01,907 --> 00:19:03,775
don't want to live with you.

310
00:19:03,876 --> 00:19:05,777
Gratitude is one thing,

311
00:19:06,011 --> 00:19:07,880
but every time I look at you,

312
00:19:08,580 --> 00:19:11,183
things I want to forget
come flooding back.

313
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:12,885
Mom.

314
00:19:13,252 --> 00:19:14,753
Either she leaves,

315
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:17,289
- or I do...
- Then you leave.

316
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:19,958
- Se Ri!
- I was frightened.

317
00:19:20,192 --> 00:19:22,194
I was truly frightened, all alone.

318
00:19:23,028 --> 00:19:24,580
You said you'd give me Seo Chon.

319
00:19:24,663 --> 00:19:26,765
You said we'd live together.
Why change your story?

320
00:19:27,866 --> 00:19:29,535
I hate that I'm being this shameless,

321
00:19:29,635 --> 00:19:32,671
but I feel pathetic
for not being able to walk away.

322
00:19:34,239 --> 00:19:35,607
I have to get to work.

323
00:19:35,807 --> 00:19:38,477
Seung Hyun, keep your promise.

324
00:19:38,810 --> 00:19:41,947
They say you shouldn't change your tune
once you've gotten what you wanted.

325
00:19:46,285 --> 00:19:47,286
What?

326
00:19:47,953 --> 00:19:49,488
Am I wrong?

327
00:19:49,655 --> 00:19:52,357
You said you'd do anything
if only O Reum lived.

328
00:19:53,392 --> 00:19:54,593
Honestly...

329
00:20:09,942 --> 00:20:12,511
My boy's hair is growing back nicely.

330
00:20:13,078 --> 00:20:14,296
The hat is hot.

331
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:15,297
- Too hot?
- Yes.

332
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:16,982
All right, take it off.

333
00:20:18,183 --> 00:20:20,452
Handsome with it, handsome without it.

334
00:20:20,619 --> 00:20:22,454
My boy is the best.

335
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:30,095
How did it go?

336
00:20:30,462 --> 00:20:31,630
How do you think it went?

337
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:32,965
She had us cornered.

338
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:34,933
Seung Woo must be furious.

339
00:20:35,067 --> 00:20:36,401
I understand why.

340
00:20:38,837 --> 00:20:40,272
I'll get ready to go to the office.

341
00:20:42,107 --> 00:20:43,208
Say "Bye, Daddy."

342
00:20:43,508 --> 00:20:44,576
Bye.

343
00:20:53,051 --> 00:20:55,020
I haven't washed up yet.

344
00:20:55,687 --> 00:20:56,888
Please hurry.

345
00:20:58,357 --> 00:20:59,791
There's only one bathroom,

346
00:20:59,891 --> 00:21:02,527
and I'd rather live alone
with my daughter...

347
00:21:30,489 --> 00:21:32,257
I think that lady made it.

348
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:34,593
Yes, I cooked today.

349
00:21:37,729 --> 00:21:38,764
Actually,

350
00:21:39,598 --> 00:21:41,133
my husband...

351
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:43,135
he eats rice with his meals.

352
00:21:44,269 --> 00:21:45,604
By the way,

353
00:21:45,737 --> 00:21:48,740
could you stop calling me "that lady?"

354
00:21:48,874 --> 00:21:50,909
Then what should I call you?

355
00:21:52,144 --> 00:21:53,812
My second mother-in-law?

356
00:21:55,681 --> 00:21:58,150
- What's so funny?
- It is funny.

357
00:21:58,750 --> 00:21:59,918
In all my life,

358
00:22:00,052 --> 00:22:01,987
I've never heard
of a second mother-in-law.

359
00:22:02,254 --> 00:22:04,556
If you don't like that, then "lady" it is.

360
00:22:05,357 --> 00:22:06,591
Well,

361
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:08,444
"Teacher,"

362
00:22:08,527 --> 00:22:10,195
or "Maestro?" How about that?

363
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:12,164
Teacher?

364
00:22:12,464 --> 00:22:13,549
This isn't a school.

365
00:22:13,632 --> 00:22:14,599
Maestro?

366
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:16,201
This isn't an orchestra.

367
00:22:16,568 --> 00:22:18,870
- Not great.
- Not you too!

368
00:22:19,037 --> 00:22:20,472
What did I do?

369
00:22:20,806 --> 00:22:23,709
I'm the one saying
Ji Ni should come over soon.

370
00:22:23,842 --> 00:22:25,844
A mother is a mother,
a daughter is a daughter.

371
00:22:26,078 --> 00:22:28,113
I learned so much through all this.

372
00:22:28,847 --> 00:22:30,048
No matter how much I love him,

373
00:22:30,148 --> 00:22:32,684
I couldn't give my own son my marrow.

374
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:36,955
That girl never listens.

375
00:22:37,322 --> 00:22:40,559
She has no idea
what I have to put up with here...

376
00:22:41,927 --> 00:22:43,328
Is O Reum asleep?

377
00:22:43,628 --> 00:22:45,063
I miss him.

378
00:22:45,697 --> 00:22:47,783
Maybe because he has my daughter's marrow.

379
00:22:47,866 --> 00:22:49,285
He feels like my own grandson.

380
00:22:49,368 --> 00:22:51,069
And he looks so much like my husband.

381
00:22:51,269 --> 00:22:54,806
I said the same thing
the first time I met him...

382
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:56,375
Did you?

383
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:59,644
If you want to stay in this house,
you'd better watch your mouth.

384
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:04,316
You give up.

385
00:23:04,850 --> 00:23:06,184
He was my husband.

386
00:23:06,318 --> 00:23:07,753
Didn't you see me at the funeral?

387
00:23:10,922 --> 00:23:12,858
That looks delicious.

388
00:23:13,091 --> 00:23:15,260
Yeong Ju, remarry.

389
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:17,079
I prayed for you to remarry...

390
00:23:17,162 --> 00:23:18,930
for 30 years.

391
00:23:19,297 --> 00:23:21,600
Find yourself a very rich man,

392
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:23,869
give me this house, and go.

393
00:23:25,370 --> 00:23:27,706
I prayed for 20 years that you'd die.

394
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:42,554
Aren't you eating breakfast?

395
00:23:42,854 --> 00:23:45,090
How could I? The atmosphere's awful.

396
00:23:45,690 --> 00:23:47,159
It doesn't feel like our home.

397
00:23:48,026 --> 00:23:50,262
You're right. It's awful.

398
00:23:50,562 --> 00:23:52,164
I was caught between them,

399
00:23:52,364 --> 00:23:53,515
so I slipped out.

400
00:23:53,598 --> 00:23:56,201
I wish only Ji Ni would come.
Not that lady.

401
00:23:57,302 --> 00:23:59,805
I'm sorry.
The house is a circus, isn't it?

402
00:24:00,572 --> 00:24:02,340
I understand now why my husband...

403
00:24:02,574 --> 00:24:05,177
had to be the man
of the house for his mother.

404
00:24:05,343 --> 00:24:07,579
At first, I wondered how that could be.

405
00:24:08,513 --> 00:24:10,148
My poor husband.

406
00:24:14,419 --> 00:24:15,420
Seung Hyun.

407
00:24:15,887 --> 00:24:17,923
- You scared me.
- What? Are you two dating?

408
00:24:18,356 --> 00:24:20,625
You're only realizing now? You're slow.

409
00:24:22,394 --> 00:24:24,095
So much for acting so generous.

410
00:24:24,196 --> 00:24:26,565
- Why aren't you eating?
- I agreed to allow it, not to like it.

411
00:24:27,165 --> 00:24:28,633
You never listen.

412
00:24:28,867 --> 00:24:30,435
- Two-faced.
- Be quiet.

413
00:24:31,570 --> 00:24:33,338
O Reum, I'm off. See you tonight.

414
00:24:33,638 --> 00:24:34,673
Take care!

415
00:24:39,544 --> 00:24:42,514
- Doctor, come out here.
- What is it?

416
00:24:51,790 --> 00:24:55,327
- They sent it like this?
- Yes, I just opened the box...

417
00:24:57,095 --> 00:24:59,231
I truly don't know
what's gotten into that old man.

418
00:24:59,397 --> 00:25:01,116
Last time the licorice root was moldy,

419
00:25:01,199 --> 00:25:03,134
and you made quite a fuss about it.

420
00:25:04,236 --> 00:25:06,338
You let it go because you pitied him...

421
00:25:13,912 --> 00:25:16,748
This is Boyak Oriental Medicine Clinic.

422
00:25:17,249 --> 00:25:19,551
We're ending our business
with you as of today.

423
00:25:19,985 --> 00:25:21,152
I don't need to give a reason.

424
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:24,222
The rainy season isn't news.
If this is how you handle storage,

425
00:25:24,422 --> 00:25:25,624
we're done here.

426
00:25:26,091 --> 00:25:27,792
Refund our advance payment immediately.

427
00:25:28,026 --> 00:25:29,427
I won't discuss this any further.

428
00:25:29,895 --> 00:25:30,962
Hello?

429
00:25:31,496 --> 00:25:32,697
Did you hang up?

430
00:25:34,399 --> 00:25:36,601
Yes, please handle it right away.

431
00:25:39,971 --> 00:25:42,407
I'll find us a new herb supplier,

432
00:25:42,641 --> 00:25:44,476
Just prepare what we need
for this week's decoctions.

433
00:25:45,510 --> 00:25:46,511
Yes.

434
00:25:51,516 --> 00:25:53,952
A gentle person is scarier when angry.

435
00:26:11,803 --> 00:26:13,738
(Mom)

436
00:26:24,916 --> 00:26:25,984
(Mom)

437
00:26:30,088 --> 00:26:31,923
Why do you keep calling?

438
00:26:45,370 --> 00:26:49,174
I'm busy. I have to use the toilet
before it gets crowded.

439
00:26:49,374 --> 00:26:51,343
That's why I'm telling you to come here.

440
00:26:51,643 --> 00:26:54,029
Who do you think I'm here for? You!

441
00:26:54,112 --> 00:26:56,381
I hate that you're living
in a commercial building.

442
00:26:58,583 --> 00:27:00,569
It's your dad's house.
Why wouldn't it concern you?

443
00:27:00,652 --> 00:27:02,153
We have O Reum.

444
00:27:02,587 --> 00:27:05,240
As long as he's here,
they can't refuse us.

445
00:27:05,323 --> 00:27:08,493
You were so against it,
and now you'd use O Reum as an excuse?

446
00:27:08,760 --> 00:27:10,095
What else can I do?

447
00:27:10,195 --> 00:27:12,964
Do you think it's easy to be consistent?

448
00:27:13,665 --> 00:27:15,233
I cleaned it over the weekend,

449
00:27:15,433 --> 00:27:17,569
and made it fit to live in,

450
00:27:17,702 --> 00:27:18,787
so come on over.

451
00:27:18,870 --> 00:27:19,971
I'm hanging up.

452
00:27:20,805 --> 00:27:22,240
Honestly.

453
00:27:23,441 --> 00:27:25,710
Kids never understand their mothers.

454
00:28:02,681 --> 00:28:05,984
(Family Register)

455
00:28:06,184 --> 00:28:07,669
I have a boyfriend.

456
00:28:07,752 --> 00:28:10,205
- Jumping to conclusions again?
- Mother's been looking pretty lately.

457
00:28:10,288 --> 00:28:12,207
- A man bought it for you.
- No.

458
00:28:12,290 --> 00:28:13,475
You know I love your paintings, right?

459
00:28:13,558 --> 00:28:14,959
But now you love Na Ji Ni's, don't you?

460
00:28:15,126 --> 00:28:16,678
Ji Ni is Ji Ni, and you are you.

461
00:28:16,761 --> 00:28:17,879
Could you please leave this house?

462
00:28:17,962 --> 00:28:19,648
Your mother was a mistress.

463
00:28:19,731 --> 00:28:21,483
Do you still not see
that you're being punished?

464
00:28:21,566 --> 00:28:22,618
Let's use some common sense.

465
00:28:22,701 --> 00:28:24,486
- This isn't our house.
- It is our house.

466
00:28:24,569 --> 00:28:26,154
I'm not leaving until I find an apartment.

467
00:28:26,237 --> 00:28:28,339
And how will you get an apartment?

468
00:28:31,076 --> 00:28:33,244
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
